From 701b37058fca719011c58c2b83944e9f60ae4630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fxzx micah <48860358+fxzxmicah@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:58:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Isolate optional protocols and daemon backends

Move encryption and Linux MD RAID operations, configuration, probing, state
and policy into independent modules. Keep ordinary block-device operations,
ATA health and maintenance, and all NVMe capabilities in the core.

Build a separate client library and introspection namespace for each storage
module. Resolve module proxies and presentation data through a common client
registry, without making applications depend on daemon backends. Give the
core client a new SONAME for the reduced public API.

Let modules own exported resources and participate in configuration, teardown
and state cleanup through common facilities. Share the daemon implementation
between the executable and its modules. Move encryption commands out of the
core CLI and compose encrypted-volume creation with ordinary filesystem
formatting through explicit interfaces.
